---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

/* The structural facts stay bound to the Russian entry — status, year, client, role
   and genres are read from the collection, never retyped for the translation. */
const source = (await getCollection("works")).find((item) => item.data.id === "work:virtualnyy-ofis-advokata");
const statusLabels: Record<string, string> = { ongoing: "Ongoing", completed: "Completed" };
const genreLabels: Record<string, string> = { xr: "XR", community: "Community", web: "Web" };
/* The catalogue stores these two fields in Russian; the page only relabels the values
   it is given — an unmapped fragment would fall through in the original wording. */
const clientLabels: Record<string, string> = { "Антон Окулов": "Anton Okulov" };
const roleLabels: Record<string, string> = {
  "Спроектировал концепцию виртуального офиса и его связку с сайтом": "Designed the concept of the virtual office and how it connects with the website",
  "Собрал пространство в Unity": "Assembled the space in Unity",
  "Использовал ProBuilder для геометрии и Spatial для публикации": "Used ProBuilder for the geometry and Spatial for publishing",
};
const status = source ? statusLabels[source.data.status] ?? source.data.status : "Completed";
const genres = source?.data.genres.map((genre) => genreLabels[genre] ?? genre) ?? [];
const year = source ? String(source.data.year).trim() : "";
const role = source ? source.data.role.split("; ").map((item) => roleLabels[item] ?? item).join(" · ") : "";
const client = source?.data.client ? clientLabels[source.data.client] ?? source.data.client : "";

const pageTitle = "Virtual office for a lawyer — an XR space for consultations and public talks";
const description = "Build a virtual office for a lawyer that works as a space for consultations, professional conversation and public talks rather than a decorative 3D location, and alongside it a personal website that works not only as a calling card but as a clear entry point into a consultation, an expert brand and a related digital service.";
const workJsonLd = {
  "@type": "CreativeWork",
  "@id": new URL("/en/works/virtualnyy-ofis-advokata/#content", Astro.site).href,
  url: new URL("/en/works/virtualnyy-ofis-advokata/", Astro.site).href,
  name: "Virtual office for a lawyer",
  headline: "Virtual office for a lawyer",
  description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  author: { "@id": new URL("/#stanislav-ermolenko", Astro.site).href },
  isPartOf: { "@id": new URL("/#website", Astro.site).href },
  ...(source?.data.updated ? { dateModified: source.data.updated.toISOString() } : {}),
};
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={description} lang="en" jsonLd={workJsonLd}>
  <article class="entry-shell">
    <header class="entry-hero">
      <div class="entry-hero-meta"><span class="section-kicker">Work · {status}</span></div>
      <h1>Virtual office for a lawyer</h1>
      <p class="entry-summary">{description}</p>
      <dl class="work-facts">
        {year && <div><dt>Year</dt><dd>{year}</dd></div>}
        {role && <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>{role}</dd></div>}
        {client && <div><dt>Client</dt><dd>{client}</dd></div>}
        {genres.length > 0 && <div><dt>Genres</dt><dd>{genres.join(" · ")}</dd></div>}
      </dl>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The brief</h2>
      <p>Create a virtual office for a lawyer that works as a space for consultations, professional conversation and public talks, rather than just a decorative 3D location. Alongside it — build a personal website that works not only as a calling card but as a clear entry point into a consultation, an expert brand and a connected digital service.</p>

      <h2>Context</h2>
      <p>The case joins XR, a social function and applied service. What matters for it is not only the form but the reason why such an office is needed at all: some users may feel safer in a virtual environment than in face-to-face communication.</p>
      <p>The context of cooperation with the Kirov AIDS centre is especially significant here. Through this office free legal consultations were planned, where the anonymity of the metaverse became not a decorative gimmick but practical value. The ability to choose an avatar and change your voice lowered the barrier to entry for people for whom confidentiality and psychological safety matter.</p>
      <p>This is also a case about packaging an expert legal service as a whole — from the website to the immersive space. The website did not live on its own but led the user towards a more unusual format of interaction, joining classic web and the metaverse into a single ecosystem.</p>

<iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/U_kap319J-U?si=IeWEwll4_1cEeeYj&amp;start=5273" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>

      <h2>Solution</h2>

      <h3>The virtual office (XR)</h3>
      <p>The virtual office was assembled in <code>Unity</code> using <code>ProBuilder</code> and published on the <code>Spatial</code> platform. The space was shaped like a lawyer&rsquo;s badge, with a panorama of Kirov, a circular balcony and a division into more open and more private zones for conversation.</p>
      <p>This was not just an XR experiment but a space with several usage scenarios: free legal consultations by prior appointment through the website, open professional discussions, interviews and other event formats.</p>

      <h3>The website (Tilda)</h3>
      <p>The lawyer&rsquo;s personal website was assembled on <code>Tilda</code>. It packaged the legal practice, gave a clear structure for getting to know the service and worked as the main entry point into the consultation scenario. From the web interface you can go into the virtual office, forming a connected digital ecosystem.</p>
      <p>In addition, the project featured an AI bot answering typical questions. For a project like this not only the visual side mattered but also the legal accuracy of the interface: consent texts, the data processing policy, the clarity of the enquiry scenario — so that the website would not promise too much or leave the client exposed over formalities.</p>

      <h2>What I did personally</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Designed the concept of the virtual office and how it connects with the website</li>
        <li>Assembled the space in Unity</li>
        <li>Used ProBuilder for the geometry and Spatial for publishing</li>
        <li>Developed the website on Tilda</li>
        <li>Thought through the zoning and the usage scenarios of the virtual office</li>
        <li>Thought through the user journey from first contact on the website to an enquiry and a consultation</li>
        <li>Took part in working out the legal and documentary layer of the website</li>
        <li>Took account of the social scenario of anonymous consultations in connection with the AIDS centre</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Stack</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Unity</li>
        <li>ProBuilder</li>
        <li>Spatial</li>
        <li>Tilda</li>
        <li>GenAI / AI bot</li>
        <li>virtual scenography</li>
        <li>consultation scenarios</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>XR production</li>
        <li>designing social spaces</li>
        <li>digital scenography</li>
        <li>translating an applied task into an immersive format</li>
        <li>expert websites</li>
        <li>UX for legal services</li>
        <li>design for trust and a personal brand</li>
        <li>connecting a website with unconventional digital formats</li>
        <li>understanding of the legal context of consultation and lead-generation websites</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Immediate focus</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Add screenshots and a video tour of the space</li>
        <li>Clarify the real usage scenarios after launch</li>
        <li>Set down why this case matters for the legal field and for the XR context</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Result</h2>
      <p>The outcome is a full-fledged digital ecosystem for a legal practice. The virtual office is a rare applied XR case where the space works not for the wow effect but for safer and more flexible communication. The personal website solves the classic task of trust and introduction to the service, yet extends into a metaverse that can be entered straight from the browser. The office was used for events, interviews and free legal consultations. This is one of the strongest works in the portfolio, at the junction of virtual worlds, social meaning and a real client scenario.</p>

      <h2>Links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://metaadvokat.ru/">https://metaadvokat.ru/</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://metaadvokat.ru/metaoffice">https://metaadvokat.ru/metaoffice</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="entry-original"><a class="text-link" href="/works/virtualnyy-ofis-advokata/">Original (Russian) →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
